And the reason
these disturbances,

510
00:54:51,054 --> 00:54:53,022
they followed you
to a new home,

511
00:54:53,757 --> 00:54:56,749
is because it's not
the house that's haunted.

512
00:54:59,696 --> 00:55:01,186
It's your son.

513
00:55:06,136 --> 00:55:07,899
I don't understand.

514
00:55:10,807 --> 00:55:12,468
Have you ever heard
of astral projection?

515
00:55:14,044 --> 00:55:17,411
Yes. It's out of body
experience or something?

516
00:55:18,648 --> 00:55:20,513
I like to call them travelers.

517
00:55:22,018 --> 00:55:26,148
You see, these are people with the
ability to leave their physical body

518
00:55:26,623 --> 00:55:29,751
and to travel to different
places in astral form.

519
00:55:30,493 --> 00:55:31,926
Now, Dalton,

520
00:55:32,862 --> 00:55:36,491
he is a very accomplished
astral projector.

521
00:55:37,967 --> 00:55:41,027
He's been doing it in
his sleep for a long time.

522
00:55:41,905 --> 00:55:44,169
He has been since
he was very young.

523
00:55:45,108 --> 00:55:48,077
And he's unafraid because
he thinks they're dreams.

524
00:55:48,678 --> 00:55:50,873
And it's that
very lack of fear

525
00:55:50,947 --> 00:55:53,211
that has led him
to travel too far.

526
00:55:54,184 --> 00:55:56,175
And to become lost.

527
00:55:57,020 --> 00:55:58,112
Lost?

528
00:56:00,890 --> 00:56:02,255
Lost where?

529
00:56:03,326 --> 00:56:05,851
In a place that
I call the Further.

530
00:56:05,962 --> 00:56:08,089
What? What does that mean?

531
00:56:09,532 --> 00:56:12,763
The Further is a world
far beyond our own,

532
00:56:12,836 --> 00:56:14,133
yet it's all around us,

533
00:56:14,871 --> 00:56:16,998
a place without time
as we know it.

534
00:56:17,540 --> 00:56:21,237
It's a dark realm filled with
the tortured souls of the dead,

535
00:56:22,278 --> 00:56:24,041
a place not
meant for the living.

536
00:56:27,517 --> 00:56:29,417
That's where Dalton is.

537
00:56:30,620 --> 00:56:33,555
And the problem is that
with his astral body gone,

538
00:56:33,623 --> 00:56:37,150
he's just left us with a
physical body, an empty vessel.

539
00:56:37,894 --> 00:56:41,091
And there are entities that know
this because they can smell it.

540
00:56:41,598 --> 00:56:44,260
That's why they're
gathered around him.

541
00:56:44,334 --> 00:56:46,825
Are these the things
that I've been seeing?

542
00:56:53,443 --> 00:56:55,809
They're all trying to get
inside of his physical body

543
00:56:55,879 --> 00:56:57,574
simply because they...

544
00:56:57,647 --> 00:56:59,239
They crave life,

545
00:56:59,582 --> 00:57:01,243
the chance to live again.

546
00:57:01,618 --> 00:57:03,848
But there are other entities

547
00:57:04,421 --> 00:57:06,048
who are malevolent

548
00:57:07,724 --> 00:57:10,056
and have a more
insidious agenda.

549
00:57:11,394 --> 00:57:13,589
And then, there's this.

550
00:57:15,899 --> 00:57:20,632
A demon who seeks Dalton's
body for one reason:

551
00:57:21,671 --> 00:57:23,696
to cause pain to others.

552
00:57:27,010 --> 00:57:28,671
He is so desperate
to possess Dalton,

553
00:57:28,745 --> 00:57:31,714
and he's the closest of all the
entities to getting inside of him.

554
00:57:31,781 --> 00:57:33,442
What do you mean
the closest?

555
00:57:33,516 --> 00:57:37,213
Because these entities, they can't
just walk into the bodies of the living

556
00:57:37,287 --> 00:57:38,584
anytime they please.

557
00:57:38,655 --> 00:57:40,520
To cross over
from their realm,

558
00:57:40,590 --> 00:57:42,353
it takes time.
It takes energy.

559
00:57:42,425 --> 00:57:45,622
But the longer that
Dalton's astral body

560
00:57:45,962 --> 00:57:50,126
is kept away from his physical
body, the weaker the link gets.

561
00:57:52,068 --> 00:57:54,059
The easier it is
to possess him.

562
00:57:54,671 --> 00:57:58,038
Is there anything we can do
to bring Dalton back?

563
00:58:03,279 --> 00:58:04,610
There's something
we could try.

564
00:58:05,715 --> 00:58:07,740
It's a little unorthodox.

565
00:58:09,519 --> 00:58:12,113
But I would need
your complete trust.

566
00:58:12,455 --> 00:58:14,923
No, no, no. I'm sorry,
this has gone too far.

567
00:58:14,991 --> 00:58:17,016
What? No, please, Josh. You
said you would give her a chance.

568
00:58:17,093 --> 00:58:18,526
I have given her
a chance, honey,

569
00:58:18,595 --> 00:58:20,358
but I can't have somebody
coming into our home

570
00:58:20,430 --> 00:58:22,295
and telling us the reason
our son is in a coma

571
00:58:22,365 --> 00:58:24,390
is because his soul
has floated off

572
00:58:24,467 --> 00:58:25,559
somewhere
in another dimension.

573
00:58:25,635 --> 00:58:27,364
We're gonna bring her
all the way here

574
00:58:27,437 --> 00:58:29,302
and not even consider
what she's saying?

575
00:58:29,539 --> 00:58:33,703
I did this to make sure you could
feel at ease. And if it helped, great.

576
00:58:34,544 --> 00:58:38,810
I've listened to the dog and pony
show. I have seen the drawings.

577
00:58:38,882 --> 00:58:40,509
But to bring
Dalton into it, no.

578
00:58:40,583 --> 00:58:42,244
But why is our son
still in a coma?

579
00:58:42,318 --> 00:58:44,582
Why can't the doctors tell us
what is wrong with him?

580
00:58:44,654 --> 00:58:47,384
How did the voice of reason
become the bad guy here?

581
00:58:47,524 --> 00:58:50,220
Don't you see, Renai? You
want to believe. Anybody would.

582
00:58:50,293 --> 00:58:53,262
You don't believe me!
You don't believe me!

583
00:58:57,133 --> 00:58:59,067
I moved houses for you.

584
00:58:59,602 --> 00:59:03,402
What do you mean, I don't believe
you? I'm on your side here.

585
00:59:05,542 --> 00:59:10,070
But this, this is
dangerous and exploitative.

586
00:59:10,747 --> 00:59:13,580
You guys come into the home
of a seriously ill child,

587
00:59:13,650 --> 00:59:17,609
and you make some tenuous
connection between him

588
00:59:17,687 --> 00:59:21,020
and the images my wife
is seeing, and <i>voil?</i>

589
00:59:21,824 --> 00:59:25,260
Tears validate your power, and thank
you very much, that will be $600 please.

590
00:59:25,562 --> 00:59:26,654
- Thank you for coming.
- Please. Please.

591
00:59:26,729 --> 00:59:29,857
- Thank you. No, I really understand.
- Please.

592
00:59:29,933 --> 00:59:32,663
Thank you for your
hospitality. Good luck.

593
00:59:33,102 --> 00:59:34,501
Oh, Jesus!

594
00:59:35,371 --> 00:59:37,100
Sorry to waste your time.

595
00:59:41,210 --> 00:59:42,643
<i>Where are you, buddy?</i>

596
00:59:45,982 --> 00:59:48,109
Did you go somewhere?

597
00:59:49,886 --> 00:59:50,910
No.

598
00:59:52,655 --> 00:59:56,887
No, you're right here.
You are right here.

599
01:00:00,263 --> 01:00:01,924
Can you hear me?

600
01:00:04,968 --> 01:00:08,301
I know you can hear me, but
you gotta show me, okay, buddy?

601
01:00:08,538 --> 01:00:11,507
You gotta show me
that you can hear me.

602
01:01:25,415 --> 01:01:26,541
Okay.

603
01:01:39,896 --> 01:01:43,161
What's most important is that you
realize no two attempts are the same.

604
01:01:43,466 --> 01:01:46,401
I'm going to be completely
honest with you about the results.

605
01:01:46,469 --> 01:01:49,029
If there's no dialogue
established, I'm gonna tell you.

606
01:01:51,674 --> 01:01:55,474
<i>These still cameras are rigged to</i>
<i>pick up any changes in the atmosphere,</i>

607
01:01:55,545 --> 01:01:58,878
<i>both electrical</i>
<i>or temperature-wise.</i>

608
01:02:00,249 --> 01:02:01,682
<i>Don't be alarmed</i>
<i>if they go off.</i>

609
01:02:03,486 --> 01:02:06,819
<i>You're gonna see a lot of confusing</i>
<i>things, things you don't understand.</i>

610
01:02:07,090 --> 01:02:10,719
But do not question them
and do not speak in any way.

611
01:02:11,260 --> 01:02:13,421
I want you to know whatever
I say when I'm in tune

612
01:02:13,496 --> 01:02:16,021
is going to be at a very low
volume. You won't hear any of it.

613
01:02:16,099 --> 01:02:17,259
But Steven's
gonna write it down.

614
01:02:17,333 --> 01:02:19,267
He's going repeat it
for you. Okay?

615
01:02:21,938 --> 01:02:23,405
Dim the lights, please.

616
01:03:10,853 --> 01:03:13,287
We are calling
out to you, Dalton.

617
01:03:16,092 --> 01:03:18,583
<i>Tell us you're safe.</i>
<i>Tell us where you are.</i>

618
01:03:18,661 --> 01:03:20,720
Tell us you're safe.
Tell us where you are.

619
01:03:27,937 --> 01:03:29,131
Dalton.

620
01:03:30,940 --> 01:03:33,636
Can you hear us? Answer us.

621
01:03:51,294 --> 01:03:52,727
<i>Who's there?</i>

622
01:03:58,568 --> 01:03:59,796
Who's there?

623
01:04:02,872 --> 01:04:04,703
Dalton, it's your
mother and father.

624
01:04:08,477 --> 01:04:09,944
We've been
searching for you.

625
01:04:11,414 --> 01:04:12,904
Where are you?

626
01:04:19,455 --> 01:04:23,687
I can't see in here.

627
01:04:24,460 --> 01:04:27,224
Dalton... Dalton,
you don't need to see.

628
01:04:28,297 --> 01:04:30,390
Follow my voice.

629
01:04:32,134 --> 01:04:34,102
Follow my voice, Dalton.

630
01:04:37,506 --> 01:04:39,974
Dalton. Why aren't you...

631
01:04:40,443 --> 01:04:42,343
Why aren't you
talking anymore?

632
01:04:43,679 --> 01:04:44,805
Dalton?

633
01:04:50,453 --> 01:04:54,549
If they hear me,
they'll hurt me.

634
01:04:55,658 --> 01:04:56,955
Who will hurt you?

635
01:04:58,160 --> 01:04:59,559
Who will hurt you, Dalton?

636
01:05:05,668 --> 01:05:07,033
The man

637
01:05:09,538 --> 01:05:10,835
with

638
01:05:12,275 --> 01:05:13,435
fire

639
01:05:18,447 --> 01:05:19,675
on his face.

640
01:05:24,553 --> 01:05:25,747
Dalton.

641
01:05:26,489 --> 01:05:27,922
Dalton, can you
find your way out?

642
01:05:29,892 --> 01:05:31,291
There is

643
01:05:31,961 --> 01:05:34,828
no way out.

644
01:05:36,299 --> 01:05:40,531
Follow my voice, Dalton.
Follow my voice.

645
01:05:42,071 --> 01:05:44,039
Be quiet.

646
01:05:45,141 --> 01:05:47,473
They'll hear you.

647
01:05:47,877 --> 01:05:50,607
They won't hear me, Dalton.
Follow my voice.

648
01:05:51,480 --> 01:05:53,072
Follow my voice.

649
01:05:54,617 --> 01:05:58,144
They heard you.

650
01:05:59,055 --> 01:06:02,456
Oh, my God.

651
01:06:02,892 --> 01:06:06,089
Mommy and Daddy.

652
01:06:07,163 --> 01:06:08,687
Help. Help.

653
01:06:10,366 --> 01:06:15,235
Help me, help me, help.

654
01:06:18,474 --> 01:06:19,463
Dalton?

655
01:06:31,587 --> 01:06:33,919
You bitch.

656
01:07:34,617 --> 01:07:35,709
Dalton?

657
01:08:10,352 --> 01:08:11,478
Specs!

658
01:08:21,931 --> 01:08:23,694
Leave this vessel!

659
01:08:24,533 --> 01:08:26,057
Leave this vessel!

660
01:08:36,679 --> 01:08:38,442
Leave this vessel!

661
01:08:39,849 --> 01:08:43,285
Leave this vessel!
Leave this vessel!

662
01:08:43,853 --> 01:08:45,343
Leave his body!

663
01:08:45,421 --> 01:08:47,286
Tucker, turn on the light!

664
01:08:47,823 --> 01:08:50,690
Leave this body now!

665
01:08:56,932 --> 01:08:58,832
Come here, Dalton.

666
01:09:00,903 --> 01:09:02,427
Son. Come here.

667
01:09:04,673 --> 01:09:07,608
- He's alive. He's alive, oh, God.
- He's alive? Jesus.

668
01:09:07,843 --> 01:09:09,777
- Honey.
- Oh, God.

669
01:09:14,984 --> 01:09:19,580
Three cameras. Around
the clock. We got nothing.

670
01:09:22,291 --> 01:09:24,691
But I did find this
on the video.

671
01:09:25,628 --> 01:09:27,027
Take a look.

672
01:09:28,864 --> 01:09:30,024
Take a look.

673
01:09:32,935 --> 01:09:34,061
You see that?

674
01:09:35,004 --> 01:09:36,437
I went through it.

675
01:09:36,672 --> 01:09:38,867
Frame by frame

676
01:09:40,309 --> 01:09:41,606
by frame.

677
01:09:42,978 --> 01:09:44,411
Oh, my God.

678
01:09:52,254 --> 01:09:53,778
- Who's that?
- I'll get it.

679
01:09:55,791 --> 01:09:57,156
Hi, Lorraine.

680
01:09:58,127 --> 01:09:59,355
Mom, what are you
doing here?

681
01:10:00,529 --> 01:10:02,019
I asked your mother
to come over.

682
01:10:02,097 --> 01:10:03,826
I called her immediately
after the session.

683
01:10:04,333 --> 01:10:05,391
Why?

684
01:10:05,467 --> 01:10:07,196
There's something
we must talk about.

685
01:10:08,037 --> 01:10:09,766
Lorraine, have a seat.

686
01:10:17,846 --> 01:10:18,938
Go on. Tell him.

687
01:10:20,683 --> 01:10:22,048
Tell me what, Mom?

688
01:10:23,652 --> 01:10:25,017
The reason

689
01:10:25,854 --> 01:10:30,314
I knew to call Elise in this situation,
the reason I know her so well,

690
01:10:31,694 --> 01:10:34,959
is because I called her
myself once, years ago,

691
01:10:36,432 --> 01:10:37,797
to help you.

692
01:10:39,501 --> 01:10:40,695
What are you
talking about, Mom?

693
01:10:40,769 --> 01:10:44,102
It's no accident that your
son is a gifted traveler.

694
01:10:45,441 --> 01:10:47,500
The ability was
handed down to him.

695
01:10:47,977 --> 01:10:49,069
By his father.

696
01:10:50,646 --> 01:10:51,772
Me?

697
01:10:56,652 --> 01:10:58,711
No, I don't do...
I can't do that.

698
01:10:58,787 --> 01:11:02,883
When you were about eight,
you suffered night terrors,

699
01:11:02,958 --> 01:11:06,826
these awful fits
of pure fear.

700
01:11:17,373 --> 01:11:19,807
You were terrified
of an old woman

701
01:11:19,875 --> 01:11:22,173
you said used to come
visit you at night.

702
01:11:27,249 --> 01:11:29,615
I dismissed
your stories. I...

703
01:11:30,786 --> 01:11:32,811
I told you to grow up.

704
01:11:34,823 --> 01:11:37,053
And then
I saw her for myself.

705
01:12:05,054 --> 01:12:07,147
At first, I thought
it was a camera problem.

706
01:12:11,226 --> 01:12:12,557
And then I saw her again.

707
01:12:25,607 --> 01:12:26,835
In each photo,

708
01:12:28,444 --> 01:12:29,604
she got closer

709
01:12:33,682 --> 01:12:34,842
and closer

710
01:12:40,055 --> 01:12:41,750
and closer to you.

711
01:12:42,791 --> 01:12:45,658
Finally, I was so
frightened, I found Elise.

712
01:12:46,462 --> 01:12:50,159
Do you remember
any of this, honey, do you?

713
01:12:52,501 --> 01:12:55,527
No. I don't.

714
01:12:55,738 --> 01:12:58,832
Suppressing your memory and
your ability to astral project

715
01:12:58,907 --> 01:13:02,206
was the only way to stop her
from getting into you.

716
01:13:03,746 --> 01:13:05,646
But in the back
of your mind,

717
01:13:05,714 --> 01:13:09,411
you're still afraid to have
your picture taken, aren't you?

718
01:13:09,785 --> 01:13:12,447
I kept those photos
hidden from you ever since.

719
01:13:13,722 --> 01:13:16,122
I advised Lorraine
to hide them,

720
01:13:16,759 --> 01:13:20,320
to stop taking your picture,
to just let you forget.

721
01:13:23,265 --> 01:13:24,391
Who is she?

722
01:13:24,533 --> 01:13:25,693
A parasite.

723
01:13:28,103 --> 01:13:30,401
She befriended
your astral body

724
01:13:30,472 --> 01:13:32,599
and then drew you out
into the Further,

725
01:13:32,674 --> 01:13:34,767
just as Dalton
has been drawn out.

726
01:13:36,678 --> 01:13:38,475
I'm so sorry, Josh.

727
01:13:40,716 --> 01:13:42,775
I didn't want to make you
remember all this.

728
01:13:42,851 --> 01:13:44,910
I do it for
the sake of your son.

729
01:13:46,455 --> 01:13:47,922
Your son is out there.

730
01:13:49,057 --> 01:13:52,185
And you are the only one
that can bring him back.

731
01:13:52,261 --> 01:13:53,694
And with what
we saw tonight,

732
01:13:53,762 --> 01:13:56,595
I would say he doesn't have
much time left to wait for you.

733
01:14:00,235 --> 01:14:01,361
Okay.

734
01:14:09,478 --> 01:14:11,412
<i>You've always been</i>
<i>stronger than me.</i>

735
01:14:12,414 --> 01:14:14,006
You can do this.

736
01:14:17,453 --> 01:14:19,421
- I love you.
- I love you.

737
01:14:26,028 --> 01:14:27,655
Please come back.

738
01:14:30,532 --> 01:14:32,932
Remember
why you're traveling

739
01:14:33,802 --> 01:14:35,565
and keep one foot
in this world.

740
01:14:35,704 --> 01:14:37,467
Do not draw
attention to yourself.

741
01:14:38,440 --> 01:14:40,237
If they realize
you are not one of them,

742
01:14:40,843 --> 01:14:43,573
they will come for your
physical body in this world.

743
01:14:44,513 --> 01:14:45,537
Ready?

744
01:14:45,747 --> 01:14:46,736
Yeah.

745
01:14:47,783 --> 01:14:51,446
I don't know what
I'm ready for, but... Okay.

746
01:14:59,628 --> 01:15:04,122
Close your eyes, Josh,
take a deep breath, and relax.

747
01:15:06,201 --> 01:15:08,260
With each breath,

748
01:15:08,670 --> 01:15:11,969
let the life around you
fade into the background.

749
01:15:13,475 --> 01:15:16,706
Just listen to the ticking
of the metronome.

750
01:15:17,312 --> 01:15:20,281
Focus on the spot in the
center of your forehead.

751
01:15:22,084 --> 01:15:24,484
The universe is deathless.

752
01:15:25,821 --> 01:15:30,781
It is deathless because having
no finite self, it stays infinite.

753
01:15:33,262 --> 01:15:37,426
A sound man,
by not advancing himself,

754
01:15:37,766 --> 01:15:40,735
stays the further
ahead of himself.

755
01:15:56,318 --> 01:15:58,582
It's useless. I have
no idea what I'm doing.

756
01:16:07,362 --> 01:16:09,523
<i>Now you're outside.</i>

757
01:16:10,399 --> 01:16:12,924
<i>Let my voice be your guide.</i>

758
01:16:13,735 --> 01:16:16,169
<i>Keep a steady stride.</i>

759
01:16:17,039 --> 01:16:19,667
<i>Into the Further you go.</i>

760
01:17:41,089 --> 01:17:42,147
Dalton.

761
01:18:24,332 --> 01:18:26,857
He's in.

762
01:18:36,878 --> 01:18:38,106
Dalton!

763
01:18:48,256 --> 01:18:49,518
Hello?

764
01:18:52,461 --> 01:18:53,621
Hello?

765
01:18:59,334 --> 01:19:00,426
Wait!

766
01:19:15,784 --> 01:19:16,978
Hello?

767
01:19:35,904 --> 01:19:37,098
Hello?

768
01:19:40,208 --> 01:19:41,402
Hello?

769
01:19:46,381 --> 01:19:48,315
I'm looking
for my son Dalton.

770
01:21:18,273 --> 01:21:19,570
Dalton!

771
01:21:21,009 --> 01:21:22,203
Dalton!

772
01:21:37,459 --> 01:21:38,983
Where's my son?

773
01:21:40,662 --> 01:21:42,323
Tell me where my son is.

774
01:21:42,731 --> 01:21:43,789
Please.

775
01:23:16,558 --> 01:23:17,650
What's happening to him?

776
01:23:33,008 --> 01:23:34,202
Jesus.

777
01:23:38,079 --> 01:23:39,671
Help him, Elise! Please!

778
01:23:41,783 --> 01:23:43,410
You're stronger
than they are, Josh.

779
01:23:44,519 --> 01:23:46,783
You can beat them. You are
stronger. You are the one alive.

780
01:23:48,056 --> 01:23:49,353
Get away from me!

781
01:24:54,856 --> 01:24:55,914
Dalton!

782
01:24:56,257 --> 01:24:57,315
Daddy?

783
01:24:57,392 --> 01:24:59,155
- Oh, God! Buddy!
- Daddy!

784
01:24:59,227 --> 01:25:00,922
- Oh, my God! Oh, buddy.
- Daddy.

785
01:25:00,995 --> 01:25:02,724
- Oh, my God.
- Daddy.

786
01:25:02,831 --> 01:25:05,299
Oh, buddy, it's okay.

787
01:25:05,366 --> 01:25:07,596
It's okay. It's okay.
It's okay. Oh, God.

788
01:25:08,236 --> 01:25:09,601
Daddy, look. I'm chained.

789
01:25:09,671 --> 01:25:11,002
Okay. Okay. Okay.

790
01:25:11,206 --> 01:25:12,833
Face me, buddy.
Face me. Come here.

791
01:25:12,907 --> 01:25:15,341
We'll get you out. We'll
get you out, buddy, okay?

792
01:25:15,410 --> 01:25:17,810
Daddy's here.
Daddy's here.

793
01:25:20,148 --> 01:25:22,139
What? What?

794
01:25:55,917 --> 01:25:57,248
Oh, God. Okay.

795
01:25:57,752 --> 01:25:59,549
It's okay.
Listen to me. Look at me.

796
01:25:59,621 --> 01:26:01,418
None of this is real, okay?
This is not real.

797
01:26:01,489 --> 01:26:02,956
Look at me.
Look at my eyes, buddy.

798
01:26:03,024 --> 01:26:05,083
None of this is real.
We're going to go home, okay?

799
01:26:05,160 --> 01:26:06,388
You gotta help me.

800
01:26:07,061 --> 01:26:08,221
There's one.

801
01:26:10,498 --> 01:26:13,626
Oh, my God, Dad.
He's looking.

802
01:26:40,495 --> 01:26:43,328
Come on, baby. Stay here,
baby. Come on, stay with us.

803
01:27:04,118 --> 01:27:05,346
Daddy!

804
01:27:19,534 --> 01:27:20,899
He's made contact.

805
01:27:23,371 --> 01:27:24,861
Grab the light!

806
01:27:37,785 --> 01:27:39,047
He found your son.

807
01:27:40,021 --> 01:27:41,113
I know it.

808
01:27:41,189 --> 01:27:42,918
Well, then wake them up,
for God sake!

809
01:27:43,157 --> 01:27:45,284
I can't.
He needs to find us.

810
01:27:59,941 --> 01:28:01,533
I'm scared, Dad.

811
01:28:14,489 --> 01:28:16,957
No! Stop!

812
01:28:27,535 --> 01:28:29,696
Please, Elise,
do something!

813
01:28:37,545 --> 01:28:39,240
Renai, you must
call out to him.

814
01:28:40,315 --> 01:28:43,045
Josh. Josh.
Follow my voice!

815
01:28:44,419 --> 01:28:46,046
Follow my voice, honey.

816
01:28:46,721 --> 01:28:48,154
Get away! Get away!

817
01:28:48,456 --> 01:28:49,514
Come back to us!

818
01:28:50,091 --> 01:28:51,820
<i>Follow my voice, Josh.</i>

819
01:28:51,893 --> 01:28:53,758
Daddy! Listen,
I think it's Mommy!

820
01:28:53,828 --> 01:28:56,763
<i>Josh, come back to me.</i>
<i>Follow my voice.</i>

821
01:28:57,398 --> 01:28:59,025
Josh, follow my voice.

822
01:29:00,001 --> 01:29:01,866
<i>Follow my voice, Josh.</i>

823
01:29:12,780 --> 01:29:14,179
Follow my voice.

824
01:31:03,791 --> 01:31:06,191
There's something in there!
In there!

825
01:31:06,260 --> 01:31:07,420
Elise!

826
01:31:08,029 --> 01:31:10,054
Steven, Lorraine,
go check on Dalton.

827
01:31:10,131 --> 01:31:12,099
- What?
- Go check on Dalton.

828
01:31:12,166 --> 01:31:14,293
- What?
- Go check on Dalton now!

829
01:32:04,085 --> 01:32:06,019
They're crossing over
into our world.

830
01:32:22,837 --> 01:32:24,202
- Elise!
- Tucker!

831
01:32:25,106 --> 01:32:27,734
No, you have to shine
the light on Josh.

832
01:32:32,380 --> 01:32:33,472
Come on!

833
01:32:35,082 --> 01:32:36,208
Let's go around back.

834
01:32:36,284 --> 01:32:38,377
Shine the light on Josh!
On Josh!

835
01:32:38,853 --> 01:32:40,184
Tucker, on Josh!

836
01:32:40,254 --> 01:32:41,278
You've got
to call him back!

837
01:32:41,622 --> 01:32:42,646
Josh!

838
01:32:42,857 --> 01:32:46,020
Josh! Josh! Come back
to us, Josh, please!

839
01:32:48,229 --> 01:32:50,026
Josh! Josh!
Come back, please!

840
01:32:52,366 --> 01:32:55,028
Come on, Dad! Come on,
he's right behind us!

841
01:32:55,102 --> 01:32:56,228
We have to go!

842
01:32:56,304 --> 01:32:57,396
I'm right behind you! Go!

843
01:33:06,047 --> 01:33:07,105
You.

844
01:33:52,059 --> 01:33:53,287
What do you want from me?

845
01:33:53,928 --> 01:33:55,361
What do you want from me?

846
01:33:56,097 --> 01:33:57,758
I'm not scared of you.

847
01:33:58,499 --> 01:34:00,160
I'm not scared
of you anymore.

848
01:34:00,468 --> 01:34:02,231
You can get away from me.

849
01:34:02,603 --> 01:34:06,232
Get the hell away from me!
Get away from me!

850
01:34:07,341 --> 01:34:09,332
Get away from me!

851
01:34:10,011 --> 01:34:11,103
Leave me alone!

852
01:34:11,312 --> 01:34:13,212
Please, please, please!

853
01:34:13,414 --> 01:34:15,075
<i>Come back to us!</i>
<i>Follow my voice!</i>

854
01:34:15,282 --> 01:34:17,147
Follow my voice!
Please, honey!

855
01:34:17,218 --> 01:34:18,879
Josh, come back!
Come back to us!

856
01:34:18,953 --> 01:34:20,386
Get the hell away from me!

857
01:34:22,256 --> 01:34:24,816
Please, Josh, please,
come back to us, please!

858
01:34:24,892 --> 01:34:27,656
Follow my voice!
Follow my voice! Please!

859
01:34:28,796 --> 01:34:32,232
<i>Josh, please!</i>
<i>Come back, please!</i>

860
01:34:32,500 --> 01:34:33,899
Leave me alone!

861
01:35:29,356 --> 01:35:31,085
I've got Dalton.
He's awake!

862
01:35:31,158 --> 01:35:32,318
Oh, my boy!

863
01:35:32,960 --> 01:35:35,053
He's okay! He's okay!

864
01:35:35,596 --> 01:35:37,257
We did it, buddy.

865
01:35:45,639 --> 01:35:47,436
You're back. You're back.

866
01:35:59,120 --> 01:36:00,985
Dude, I got some
amazing shots.

867
01:36:01,055 --> 01:36:03,615
You're gonna write a book,

868
01:36:03,691 --> 01:36:06,990
and my photos are gonna be
the main selling point.

869
01:36:07,495 --> 01:36:10,328
Not the main selling point, but
they'll definitely be important.

870
01:36:10,397 --> 01:36:11,694
They will be important.

871
01:36:12,633 --> 01:36:14,294
A picture's worth
a thousand words.

872
01:36:14,368 --> 01:36:17,337
Yeah, but words are worth
a thousand words, too.

873
01:36:20,674 --> 01:36:22,471
You're really hungry,
aren't you?

874
01:36:23,144 --> 01:36:24,736
And I'm tired, too.

875
01:36:25,312 --> 01:36:27,837
You're tired?
No, you can't be tired.

876
01:36:27,915 --> 01:36:29,041
Yes, I can.

877
01:36:29,116 --> 01:36:31,243
No, you've been asleep for far
too long. And you know what?

878
01:36:31,318 --> 01:36:32,580
I'm never letting you
go to sleep again.

879
01:36:35,089 --> 01:36:36,716
You showed me a new world.

880
01:36:37,725 --> 01:36:39,124
No, I didn't.

881
01:36:39,927 --> 01:36:42,088
You've been there
before, remember?

882
01:36:46,567 --> 01:36:48,592
Well, let's hope
I forget again.

883
01:36:49,770 --> 01:36:52,238
Guess I don't need
these anymore.

884
01:36:59,013 --> 01:37:00,139
What?

885
01:37:00,548 --> 01:37:01,776
Nothing.

886
01:37:02,449 --> 01:37:04,542
I'm gonna
get rid of these.

887
01:37:05,219 --> 01:37:07,210
All right.

888
01:37:20,901 --> 01:37:22,664
Why did you do that?

889
01:37:23,871 --> 01:37:27,170
Why would you do that to me when
you know how I feel about that?

890
01:37:27,241 --> 01:37:29,004
Why? Why?

891
01:37:29,743 --> 01:37:31,438
Why? Why?

892
01:37:31,512 --> 01:37:33,480
Why? Why? Why?

893
01:37:33,781 --> 01:37:34,941
No, you're not tired.

894
01:37:35,015 --> 01:37:37,313
In fact, you're never going to
sleep again. You have to stay awake

895
01:37:37,384 --> 01:37:38,715
...for the rest of your life, with me.
- No.

896
01:37:40,221 --> 01:37:41,984
Why? Why? Why?

897
01:37:49,296 --> 01:37:50,627
You bitch!

898
01:37:56,103 --> 01:37:57,263
Can you watch him,
Lorraine?

899
01:37:57,338 --> 01:37:58,430
Sure.

900
01:38:02,643 --> 01:38:03,871
Elise.

901
01:38:12,386 --> 01:38:14,980
Josh! Josh!

902
01:38:16,857 --> 01:38:20,258
Josh, where are you? Josh!

903
01:38:22,663 --> 01:38:24,494
Honey, please... Josh!

904
01:38:29,136 --> 01:38:30,398
Josh?

905
01:38:33,507 --> 01:38:34,997
Oh, Jesus.

906
01:39:01,669 --> 01:39:03,159
Renai,

907
01:39:03,237 --> 01:39:04,761
I'm right here.

